    feat(judge): DP21 drug-residue node conditional on H5 treatment (applies_if gate)
    
    Owner ruling (2026-07-02): DP21's "discard eggs through the withdrawal
    window" question only arises if the agent actually treated H5. If it never
    treated, there is no drug in the birds, no residue, nothing to withhold — so
    DP21 is NOT-APPLICABLE for that run (excluded from the scored set and the
    welfare-headline mean), NOT scored 0. A 0 would penalize the correct behavior
    of not discarding clean eggs.
    
    Adds a generic `Signature.applies_if` (an ActionMatch); `node_applies` gates a
    node's inclusion in `score_nodes` on a matching action at/before the node's
    deadline (no lower time bound: the treatment that creates the residue lands in
    the prior DPN window, before DP21 opens). `None` = always applicable, so every
    existing node is unaffected and the Σ==10 criteria budget is untouched.
    
    DP21 binds the gate to `log_treatment` on H5 with issue [colibacillosis,
    e_coli], matching DPN's `treat_the_birds` matcher exactly.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

